{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" only model what a screen is showing right now — Empty, Loading, Data, or Error. They don’t know, and don’t need to know, how the screen got there. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"},{"type":"text","text":" is a separate, independent type for exactly that: was the screen freshly pushed, revealed by popping something off a navigation stack, presented modally, opened from a deep link, or launched from a Home Screen shortcut?"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates can’t detect any of this on its own — there’s no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStack"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier or UIKit push interception behind "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource"},{"type":"text","text":". Your app already knows the answer wherever navigation actually happens (a coordinator, a router, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStack"},{"type":"text","text":" path change, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onOpenURL"},{"type":"text","text":", a shortcut-item handler), so it passes the value in explicitly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-concrete-example","type":"heading","text":"A concrete example","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The most common reason to care about this: skip a reload when the user is merely returning to a screen that’s alre